  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="c2d0-a5a4-68f4-3a99" name="Late Republican Roman Consular Army (Spartacus) - List Notes" publicationId="eb14-e889-c793-0fc4" hidden="false">
      <description>LATE REPUBLICAN ROMAN CONSULAR ARMY (Spartacus, pp.15-17). The minimum size for a regiment is five models, with no upper limit; one model in each unit may be upgraded to Leader (+5 pts), Standard Bearer (+5 pts) and Musician (+5 pts). If any Roman characters are accompanying Roman units that are Drilled or Stubborn it is assumed the characters receive the same abilities automatically at no additional points cost. During the Late Republic Roman citizenship had been extended to much of the Italian peninsula so any quickly raised domestic troops were equipped and trained as legionaries; the Auxiliaries and Support Troops are presented for other theatres and may represent Numidians, Spanish, Balearics, Gauls, Cisalpine Gauls, Thracians or even Germans.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Late Republican Roman Consular Army]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Conscript Legionaries: at least 25%
  Experienced Legionaries: up to 25%
  Auxiliaries &amp; Support Troops: up to 20%
  Characters up to 25%. Legionaries: at least 25% must be Conscripts; up to 25% may be Experienced Legionaries. Auxiliaries and Support Troops up to 20% (one Scorpion per 1,000 points). If a consul is not chosen a Praetor may be made General (+25 pts). Designed for the Roman armies used in the Third Servile War; may also be used for other local municipal forces in the late Republic.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
